      "writtenOn": "2021-08-18T19:46:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I read the code changes before reading this comment and independently arrived at the same conclusions you did. We\u0027ve named all the samplers as nouns, and they don\u0027t feel like functions, but that\u0027s just a naming choice. We can fix it.\n\nIn the specific example you mention, `colorizer`-\u003e`colorize` and `gradLayout`-\u003e`layoutGradient` would probably improve it further.\n\nWe probably want to come up with a new convention for common cases like reading a texture. `image(coords)` definitely feels off. My C++ brain wants it to be like\n\n    sample(image, coords) --\u003e image.sample(coords) \n\nbut that\u0027s foreign syntax to SkSL and not worth introducing.\n\nIn general though I like this and it\u0027s IMO worth it to eliminate sample.",
      "parentUuid": "80fa4161_1a7345a8",
      "revId": "7c934cb85d8787a83424f9285bbf3d18d969c82e",
